{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The men were afraid.</b> It is written with two yods, and its Targum is וּדְחִילוּ." "<b>Because they were brought to Joseph's house.</b> And the way of other arrivals is not to buy grain for them in Joseph's house, but only in the lodgings in the city. <b>The men were afraid.</b> That this is nothing but to gather them into custody." "<b>We are being brought.</b> Into the inside of this house." "<b>To roll upon.</b> To have the accusation of the money rolled upon us and to have it fall upon us. And Onkelos, who translated וּלְאִסְתַּקָּפָא עֲלָנָא — that is the language of לְהִתְעוֹלֵל, as we translate עֲלִילַת דְּבָרִים — תַּסְקוּפֵי מִלִּין; and he did not translate according to the language of Scripture, לְהִתְגוֹלֵל, which he would have rendered לְאִתְרַבְרָבָא — that is the language of גֻּלַּת הַזָּהָב (Ecclesiastes 12), and וְהֻצַּב גֻּלְּתָה הֹעֲלָתָה (Nahum 2), which is the language of kingship."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:24.343917633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}